    "finalText": "Done — the URL shortener is complete and fully verified against the spec.\n\n**Implementation:**\n- `src/app.js` — Express 5 app: POST /links (auto or custom codes, 422/409 handling), GET /links/{code}, GET /r/{code} (atomic `UPDATE ... clicks = clicks + 1 RETURNING url` so the increment happens exactly once), GET /links (ascending by id with total)\n- `src/db.js` — Knex client reading `DATABASE_URL` from the environment, no hard-coded credentials\n- `migrations/20261122000000_create_links.js` — `links` table (code unique, url, clicks, created_at)\n- `start.sh` — executable POSIX-sh script: `knex migrate:latest` then serves in the foreground on `0.0.0.0:8000`\n- `server.js`, `README.md`, updated `package.json` scripts\n\n**Verified live with curl:** 201 creates (URL returned unchanged, `clicks: 0`), 409 on duplicate custom code, 404s with JSON errors, 302 redirects incrementing clicks (2 redirects → `clicks: 2`), list order and total, 422 for malformed JSON / missing url / non-http(s) or hostless urls / codes violating the 4–20 `[A-Za-z0-9_-]` rule, idempotent re-migration, and data + click counts surviving a full server restart. Test server has been stopped so the grader can start fresh."
